{"id": "sdqa0009", "pool": "sdqa", "tier": "conservative", "audio_s": 6.27, "n_chunks": 7, "n_concurrent": 7, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.3609, "eot_read_ms": 19, "reference_answer": "Kakapo", "query": "What is the largest parrot in New Zealand?", "transcript": "What is the largest parrot in New Zealand?", "mode": "local", "answer": "The largest parrot in New Zealand is the Kakapo. It's a very special and unique bird. The Kakapo is flightless, which means it can't fly, and it has a round body with soft feathers. It lives mainly on islands around New Zealand to stay safe from predators. One of its most interesting features is that it makes a low, owl-like hooting sound instead of chirping like many other birds. Because there are so few left—only about 200 or so in the wild—it's considered endangered and needs careful protection by conservationists.", "answer_ms": 2432}
