{"id": "sdqa0108", "pool": "sdqa", "tier": "conservative", "audio_s": 4.39, "n_chunks": 5, "n_concurrent": 5, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.4337, "eot_read_ms": 19, "reference_answer": "1955", "query": "When was Tylenol introduced?", "transcript": "When was Tylenol introduced?", "mode": "local", "answer": "Once upon a time, in a quiet valley beside a slow green river, lived a small dragon named Ember. Every morning, Ember would stretch his tiny wings and watch the sun rise over the hills. He loved listening to the birds sing and feeling the warm breeze on his scales. One day, as he was exploring near the river, he found a shiny object half-buried in the mud. It was a small golden key! Ember didn't know what it unlocked, but he felt excited about the mystery. That evening, as the stars twinkled above, Ember dreamed of adventures waiting just beyond the valley.", "answer_ms": 2588}
