{"id": "sdqa0126", "pool": "sdqa", "tier": "conservative", "audio_s": 2.49, "n_chunks": 3, "n_concurrent": 3, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.0471, "eot_read_ms": 19, "reference_answer": "the process of encoding a message or information in such a way that only authorized parties can access it and those who are not authorized cannot", "query": "What is encryption?", "transcript": "What is encryption?", "mode": "local", "answer": "Encryption is a way of protecting information by scrambling it so that only people with the right \"key\" can read it. Imagine you write a secret message, but before sending it, you use a special code to change all the letters into something that looks like nonsense. Only the person who knows the code can turn it back into your original message. This helps keep your data safe from anyone who might try to steal or read it without permission.", "answer_ms": 1806}
